# Normalize line endings: commit as LF, check out as LF on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system gitconfig, so without
# an explicit attribute every text file checks out CRLF. That silently breaks
# each script that matches lines exactly — scripts/release/stamp-release-version.mjs
# ("Cargo.toml is missing [workspace.package] version"),
# scripts/release/test-release-workflow-contract.mjs ("missing workflow section"), and
# scripts/actions/test-action-contract.mjs ("action.yml name line must be exactly ...").
# Those failures name the file, not the line endings, so they read as defects in
# perfectly intact files and make `make ci` unrunnable on a Windows checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
